// P8: genuinely unbounded input (analyzed WITHOUT any input bound).
// n starts as [-oo, +oo]; after widening the induction variable i also has an
// infinite upper bound.  The analysis is forbidden from treating the unknown
// interval as safe and must report possible OOB.  The differential harness
// additionally runs every concrete n in a bounded window [0, 7] to check
// soundness (those faults are real for n >= 3); the static result without
// bounds demonstrates "unknown is not safe" directly.
input n;
arr a[3] = [1, 2, 3];
var i = 0;
while (i < n) {
  a[i] = i;
  i = i + 1;
}
